    {
      "path": "scripts/build_site_data.py",
      "bytes": 6392,
      "sha256": "35565ad98f428ca797bb03203d555147d8e1ded831c19ab5a2d1d49a3b20f58b",
      "module_doc": "Generate site/corpus.js, the data behind the project page's paper explorer.\n\n    python3 scripts/build_site_data.py          # rewrite site/corpus.js\n    python3 scripts/build_site_data.py --check  # exit 1 if it is out of date\n\nREADME.md stays the single source of truth for entries; docs/reported-evidence.md\nfor verdicts. The page never carries a hand-edited copy of either, so an entry\nadded to the list reaches the explorer only through this script, and\ncheck_consistency.py fails if the generated file has drifted.",
      "definitions": [
        "inline_markdown",
        "read_verdicts",
        "read_entries",
        "render",
        "main"
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "scripts/check_consistency.py",
      "bytes": 12839,
      "sha256": "841240eb396173157ee11c27f27799a17a95d99a720b76b840cd5f3a04127269",
      "module_doc": "Check the invariants this list promises, so a drift fails loudly instead of quietly.\n\n    python3 scripts/check_consistency.py          # structure only, no network\n    python3 scripts/check_consistency.py --links  # also resolve every URL\n\nSix checks, each one a defect found in a comparable list rather than a\nhypothetical: a table of contents whose anchors no longer resolve, an entry\nlisted twice, two language versions that have drifted apart, a heading that\ncarries an emoji and so breaks the anchor a hand-written link points at, a\nfile that nothing links to, and a project-page explorer generated from an\nolder README. Exit status is non-zero if any check fails.",
      "definitions": [
        "read",
        "slug",
        "entry_lines",
        "entries",
        "strip_code",
        "check_anchors",
        "check_emoji_headings",
        "check_duplicates",
        "check_parity",
        "check_files",
        "check_site_data",
        "check_evidence_and_taxonomy",
        "check_citation",
        "check_paper_snapshot",
        "check_html",
        "check_links",
        "main"
      ]
    },
